<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37675" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξυβρίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>break out into insolence, wax wanton,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pherecyd.Syr.
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.146
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				7.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπραγίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ πλούτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					8.6.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐς τόδε</span>
			<i>come</i> to this pitch <i>of insolence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.39
			</span></i>: with neut. Adj. or Pron., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντοῖα ἐ.</span>
			<i>commit</i> all kinds of <i>violence</i> or <i>extravagance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδ᾽ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					293
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πλείω περὶ τοὺς θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Fug.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Phoc.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eus.Mynd.
				54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ant.Lib.
				21.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.
			pers., <i>treat with insolence</i> or <i>violence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				12.2
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοὺς ἔρωτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Conon
					24.2
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πόλις ὑφ᾽ ὑμῶν -ίζετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Phil.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -ισμένα</span>
			<i>despised</i> things, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				43.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of the body,
				<i>break out</i> from high feeding, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				691c
			</span></i>; of plants, <i>to be over-luxuriant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				725b35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.16.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἐξυβρίσαντα τὸν δῆμον ἀναφῦσαι
					πλῆθος συκοφαντῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arist.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
